WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:04.167
-Welcome back to
"The Tonight Show."

00:00:04.167 --> 00:00:07.300
It is time to play
a game of deception called

00:00:07.300 --> 00:00:09.400
"True Confessions."

00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:11.400
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:00:16.934 --> 00:00:20.234
My first opponent tonight is an
incredibly talented actress,

00:00:20.234 --> 00:00:22.834
whose new movie,
"Enola Holmes 2,"

00:00:22.834 --> 00:00:24.834
comes out on Netflix
November 4th.

00:00:24.834 --> 00:00:27.434
Please welcome
Millie Bobby Brown!

00:00:27.434 --> 00:00:29.234
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:00:29.234 --> 00:00:31.267
Hi! Perfect.

00:00:31.267 --> 00:00:33.634
That's Millie Bobby Brown!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:35.601 --> 00:00:38.033
Millie, nice.
You came right in there.

00:00:38.033 --> 00:00:40.167
Millie and I will be
facing off against

00:00:40.167 --> 00:00:42.400
one of her co-stars on
"Stranger Things."

00:00:42.400 --> 00:00:45.234
Please welcome the one-and-only
Noah Schnapp!

00:00:45.234 --> 00:00:48.234
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:00:48.234 --> 00:00:51.701
-Yeah!

00:00:51.701 --> 00:00:53.234
-Don't get scalded
by the coffee.

00:00:53.234 --> 00:00:55.634
You okay, buddy?
You came in hot, buddy. Wow.

00:00:55.634 --> 00:00:57.767
-I did not expect that.
-Yeah, came in hot there.

00:00:57.767 --> 00:00:59.133
Alright, perfect.
Alright, here's how this works.

00:00:59.133 --> 00:01:01.167
-I'm so sorry.
-No, it's too late now.

00:01:01.167 --> 00:01:03.501
-Only Noah.
-Alright.

00:01:03.501 --> 00:01:05.367
In front of each of us...

00:01:05.367 --> 00:01:06.501
[ Laughter ]

00:01:06.501 --> 00:01:08.501
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:11.234 --> 00:01:13.601
In front of each of us

00:01:13.601 --> 00:01:16.200
are two envelopes
containing confessions.

00:01:16.200 --> 00:01:17.968
One is true.

00:01:17.968 --> 00:01:19.567
The other is a lie.

00:01:19.567 --> 00:01:20.934
Once you read your confession,

00:01:20.934 --> 00:01:23.067
the other two players
get to interrogate you.

00:01:23.067 --> 00:01:24.968
Then you have to come
to a unanimous decision --

00:01:24.968 --> 00:01:26.334
is it a truth or a lie?

00:01:26.334 --> 00:01:27.634
Millie,
you're going to go first.

00:01:27.634 --> 00:01:30.000
Which envelope should she open?
What do you think?

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:31.267
1 or 2?
-Oh, we pick?

00:01:31.267 --> 00:01:32.367
-Yeah, or the audience
could pick.

00:01:32.367 --> 00:01:33.534
What do you think?
-2.

00:01:33.534 --> 00:01:35.367
[ Indistinct shouting ]
2!

00:01:35.367 --> 00:01:38.467
-Everyone said 2.
I don't know why.

00:01:38.467 --> 00:01:42.567
-I sneak my pet bunny
into hotels.

00:01:42.567 --> 00:01:44.400
♪♪

00:01:44.400 --> 00:01:45.634
-That's...

00:01:45.634 --> 00:01:48.234
-You know Millie very well.

00:01:48.234 --> 00:01:51.767
-I think that sounds
like it could be real.

00:01:51.767 --> 00:01:53.467
-Why would you sneak your bunny?

00:01:53.467 --> 00:01:54.968
Why can't you just check it in?

00:01:54.968 --> 00:01:56.534
-Millie is, like,
obsessed with animals.

00:01:56.534 --> 00:01:58.534
-Alright. But why do you
have to sneak it in?

00:01:58.534 --> 00:02:02.133
-Because, usually,
they let in dogs and cats,

00:02:02.133 --> 00:02:05.234
but probably not a rabbit.

00:02:05.234 --> 00:02:07.033
You know?

00:02:07.033 --> 00:02:09.734
It might become an issue.
-What do you mean?

00:02:09.734 --> 00:02:11.501
Because that feels like --
Well, you would know

00:02:11.501 --> 00:02:13.868
it's an issue, right, if you
already -- If you tried --

00:02:13.868 --> 00:02:16.234
-I feel like Millie, though,
wouldn't be sneaky about it.

00:02:16.234 --> 00:02:17.367
She would just walk in.

00:02:17.367 --> 00:02:18.701
-Yeah, because
she just loves animals.

00:02:18.701 --> 00:02:19.701
Yeah, she would just
walk in and say,

00:02:19.701 --> 00:02:20.868
"Hey, I have my bunny with me."

00:02:20.868 --> 00:02:22.767
-Yeah, she wouldn't care.
-Everyone loves you.

00:02:22.767 --> 00:02:24.167
Everyone would let you in
with anything.

00:02:24.167 --> 00:02:26.300
You can go in with a chainsaw
and like,

00:02:26.300 --> 00:02:28.100
"Yeah, I'm going to go to
my room with a chainsaw."

00:02:28.100 --> 00:02:30.133
They'd go, "Millie, come on in.
We love you."

00:02:30.133 --> 00:02:31.734
-Maybe.
-I don't think --

00:02:31.734 --> 00:02:33.501
-I'm saying lie.
-Oh, wait. Whoa, whoa. Wait.

00:02:33.501 --> 00:02:34.868
-But then I've got to
pay a deposit

00:02:34.868 --> 00:02:36.667
if he does something, right?

00:02:36.667 --> 00:02:38.367
It's like, uh,
do I really want to do that?

00:02:38.367 --> 00:02:40.667
No.

00:02:40.667 --> 00:02:42.801
-She's so lying.
Are you kidding me?

00:02:42.801 --> 00:02:44.334
She's such a liar.
-Why would you stay in a hotel?

00:02:44.334 --> 00:02:46.467
Don't you live in England?

00:02:46.467 --> 00:02:48.467
-I do, but I was
filming in the city.

00:02:48.467 --> 00:02:50.934
-No, this is --
I know when she's acting.

00:02:50.934 --> 00:02:52.067
This is a lie.

00:02:52.067 --> 00:02:54.567
-This is a
total, complete, absolute lie.

00:02:54.567 --> 00:02:56.968
-Like, you can't even try.
-You can't even describe this.

00:02:56.968 --> 00:02:58.200
This is such a lie.

00:02:58.200 --> 00:03:00.100
Tell us right now --
truth or lie?

00:03:00.100 --> 00:03:01.400
[ Drumroll ]

00:03:01.400 --> 00:03:02.501
-It's the truth.
-No!

00:03:02.501 --> 00:03:04.601
-Oh, come on!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:04.601 --> 00:03:06.601
[ Buzzer ]

00:03:10.701 --> 00:03:11.801
-Guys!
-You played us.

00:03:11.801 --> 00:03:13.033
-Why did I come here?
-Dude!

00:03:13.033 --> 00:03:14.234
-You played us like
a deck of cards.

00:03:14.234 --> 00:03:15.968
-Wait.
I said truth from the beginning.

00:03:15.968 --> 00:03:17.534
-Yeah, you did say -- Yeah.
-I knew it.

00:03:17.534 --> 00:03:19.601
My instincts said true.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:03:19.601 --> 00:03:22.267
-Yeah, no. It's a true story.
And it did become an issue.

00:03:22.267 --> 00:03:23.434
Like, they guy --

00:03:23.434 --> 00:03:24.767
-Did they find it?
-They did.

00:03:24.767 --> 00:03:27.901
I went into the elevator
and I put him under my sweater.

00:03:27.901 --> 00:03:30.167
And if they ask,
"I'm breast-feeding my child.

00:03:30.167 --> 00:03:33.300
Why would you ever ask me?

00:03:33.300 --> 00:03:36.701
That's so inappropriate.
Where's your H.R. lady?"

00:03:36.701 --> 00:03:37.934
Anyways...

00:03:37.934 --> 00:03:40.801
And then, he buzzes
when he gets really happy,

00:03:40.801 --> 00:03:42.367
and he was buzzing
under my shirt.

00:03:42.367 --> 00:03:44.133
And his ear came out
of my shirt,

00:03:44.133 --> 00:03:45.234
and the guy looks.

00:03:45.234 --> 00:03:49.400
And I went, "Look away."
And I got off.

00:03:49.400 --> 00:03:51.267
And then I put on my
"do not disturb" sign

00:03:51.267 --> 00:03:53.300
on my door for like five days.

00:03:53.300 --> 00:03:54.834
-So you did get away with it.
-I did, I did, yeah.

00:03:54.834 --> 00:03:56.901
-Oh, my God. Alright.
Good job. Congrats.

00:03:56.901 --> 00:03:57.934
Good on you.
You got points for that one.

00:03:57.934 --> 00:03:59.000
Alright.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:59.000 --> 00:04:02.000
Alright. It's my turn.

00:04:02.000 --> 00:04:03.934
Which envelope should I open?

00:04:03.934 --> 00:04:06.434
-Oh, my God!
[ Indistinct shouting ]

00:04:06.434 --> 00:04:07.567
Dude!

00:04:09.901 --> 00:04:10.901
-1.

00:04:10.901 --> 00:04:11.901
-1.
-1.

00:04:11.901 --> 00:04:13.200
-We'll go with 1.

00:04:13.200 --> 00:04:14.300
-Okay, be careful, 'cause I
don't want to be able

00:04:14.300 --> 00:04:15.534
to see through -- Okay.

00:04:15.534 --> 00:04:16.968
Oh, yeah, it doesn't matter.
It doesn't matter.

00:04:16.968 --> 00:04:19.167
Yeah, yeah. I got worried.

00:04:19.167 --> 00:04:23.567
-LeBron James called me
from the court during a game.

00:04:23.567 --> 00:04:26.067
-That's so cool.
-That's really cool.

00:04:26.067 --> 00:04:28.934
I think it's almost
too cool...for you.

00:04:28.934 --> 00:04:31.701
-For me?
[ Laughter ]

00:04:33.434 --> 00:04:34.567
-That's so funny.

00:04:34.567 --> 00:04:37.400
"I think it's almost
too cool...for you."

00:04:37.400 --> 00:04:39.400
Yeah.
-Okay. When?

00:04:39.400 --> 00:04:40.767
-This was probably about
four years ago.

00:04:40.767 --> 00:04:41.834
-Who were they playing?
-Oh, four years ago?

00:04:41.834 --> 00:04:43.133
-They were playing the Nuggets.

00:04:43.133 --> 00:04:44.601
Or, no, the Warriors.
The Warriors.

00:04:44.601 --> 00:04:45.934
Golden State Warriors.

00:04:45.934 --> 00:04:47.367
-What did you talk about?

00:04:47.367 --> 00:04:48.434
-What do you mean?
They didn't have a chat.

00:04:48.434 --> 00:04:49.501
He was just --
-He called you.

00:04:49.501 --> 00:04:50.534
Well, he called you.
Did you answer?

00:04:50.534 --> 00:04:53.033
-Yes, I did.
-And what did you say?

00:04:53.033 --> 00:04:54.467
-So, what happened was,
I went --

00:04:54.467 --> 00:04:55.968
-You're lying.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:55.968 --> 00:04:58.400
-Yeah, he's lying.

00:05:00.067 --> 00:05:01.334
-I feel like I almost --
-I'm going to take this.

00:05:01.334 --> 00:05:03.033
I'm gonna dip this in
a little bit more coffee

00:05:03.033 --> 00:05:04.501
and let you think.

00:05:04.501 --> 00:05:06.267
Think it over.
-Okay, what do we say?

00:05:06.267 --> 00:05:07.734
-Ew!
-What do we say?

00:05:07.734 --> 00:05:09.033
What do we say? What do we say?
-What is that?

00:05:09.033 --> 00:05:11.434
-Alright, together.

00:05:11.434 --> 00:05:12.734
-It's a lie.
-It's a lie.

00:05:12.734 --> 00:05:13.734
[ Drumroll ]

00:05:13.734 --> 00:05:15.634
-It is a lie, yeah.
[ Dinging ]

00:05:15.634 --> 00:05:17.968
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:05:18.033 --> 00:05:20.133
-Yes!
-He would never do that.

00:05:20.133 --> 00:05:22.501
He would never do that.
-Never do that.

00:05:22.501 --> 00:05:24.133
-He would never do that
during a game.

00:05:24.133 --> 00:05:25.267
You knew it.

00:05:25.267 --> 00:05:28.000
Noah, it is your turn.
Noah, which one?

00:05:28.000 --> 00:05:30.667
-1!
-Okay, 1.

00:05:30.667 --> 00:05:32.701
-Come on, bud. We got this.

00:05:32.701 --> 00:05:35.634
Enola, let's put our
detective skills to the test.

00:05:35.634 --> 00:05:37.601
-I guilt-tripped Shawn Mendes

00:05:37.601 --> 00:05:40.200
into following me back
on Instagram.

00:05:41.334 --> 00:05:42.667
-This is something he would do.

00:05:42.667 --> 00:05:44.200
-It sounds like something --
Yeah, it sounds like --

00:05:44.200 --> 00:05:45.334
When is this?

00:05:45.334 --> 00:05:47.067
-A year or two ago.

00:05:47.067 --> 00:05:48.300
-Okay, why did you
guilt-trip him?

00:05:48.300 --> 00:05:49.601
He didn't want to follow you?

00:05:49.601 --> 00:05:52.434
-Well, he followed everyone else
in the cast except me.

00:05:52.434 --> 00:05:53.868
-Shawn Mendes?

00:05:53.868 --> 00:05:57.334
-Yeah. He followed you, Sadie,
Gaten, Caleb -- everybody.

00:05:57.334 --> 00:06:00.100
-Oh, he's bitter.
-What's his problem?

00:06:00.100 --> 00:06:01.634
-Yeah, he's mad.
-This is real.

00:06:01.634 --> 00:06:02.901
-And I was like, "What the heck?

00:06:02.901 --> 00:06:04.200
Why does he
follow everyone but me?"

00:06:04.200 --> 00:06:05.601
-Yeah, what's
Shawn Mendes' problem?

00:06:05.601 --> 00:06:07.267
-You're lying.
-He has beef with me.

00:06:07.267 --> 00:06:09.501
-So, then how did you
get ahold of Shawn Mendes?

00:06:09.501 --> 00:06:11.100
-I DM'd him and I was like,
"I'm low-key offended.

00:06:11.100 --> 00:06:12.200
Why do you follow everyone --"

00:06:12.200 --> 00:06:13.400
-Did you say,
"I'm low-key offended"?

00:06:13.400 --> 00:06:14.734
You said that to him?

00:06:14.734 --> 00:06:16.167
-You can't DM someone
if they're not following you.

00:06:16.167 --> 00:06:17.334
He's lying!

00:06:17.334 --> 00:06:19.367
-No, no, no.
Jimmy, that's not -- Jimmy...

00:06:19.367 --> 00:06:21.367
[ Laughter ]

00:06:25.968 --> 00:06:28.133
-Wait, am I -- Did I just
show how old I am?

00:06:28.133 --> 00:06:30.000
-He showed his age there.
-Shh.

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:32.901
-Okay. I thought you had to
follow each other to DM.

00:06:32.901 --> 00:06:34.868
-No!
-No, you can DM anybody.

00:06:34.868 --> 00:06:38.567
-You can DM anybody?
-Jimmy, Jimmy, stop.

00:06:38.567 --> 00:06:40.300
You need to stop.

00:06:40.300 --> 00:06:43.167
-I'm not even on --
I'm on BeReal now.

00:06:43.167 --> 00:06:45.534
-Oh, he's so hip.
-I don't even care.

00:06:45.534 --> 00:06:48.667
-What did he say?
-Yeah, what did "Men-Men" say?

00:06:48.667 --> 00:06:52.467
-He said, "Oh, what's up, man.
Like, I love you so much."

00:06:52.467 --> 00:06:54.801
-He does say, "What's up, man?"
He does use the word "man."

00:06:54.801 --> 00:06:56.634
He's like, "Hey, man."
He's Canadian.

00:06:56.634 --> 00:06:58.868
-He's a fellow Canadian.
And he was like --

00:06:58.868 --> 00:07:00.868
-Shawn -- Well,
he's a very nice guy, Shawn.

00:07:00.868 --> 00:07:02.267
-Oh, I'm sweating.

00:07:02.267 --> 00:07:04.567
-When is the last time you
talked to Shawn on Instagram?

00:07:04.567 --> 00:07:06.834
-I called him the other day.
-Oh.

00:07:06.834 --> 00:07:10.100
-That is absolutely --
This such a lie.

00:07:10.100 --> 00:07:11.801
-Yeah.
-That was what -- That's it.

00:07:11.801 --> 00:07:13.334
It's over. It's over.
-It's a lie.

00:07:13.334 --> 00:07:14.868
-You called him the other day?

00:07:14.868 --> 00:07:17.467
Why would you call him if you
have him on -- If you're DMing?

00:07:17.467 --> 00:07:18.834
I'm going to say it's a lie.
-It's a lie.

00:07:18.834 --> 00:07:19.901
-It's a lie.
-It's a lie.

00:07:19.901 --> 00:07:21.400
-It's...the truth.

00:07:21.400 --> 00:07:24.400
-What?!
♪♪

00:07:24.400 --> 00:07:25.801
[ Buzzer ]

00:07:25.801 --> 00:07:27.267
Wow!

00:07:27.267 --> 00:07:30.234
Wow! Acting. Acting.

00:07:30.234 --> 00:07:32.467
Mastermind. Noah Schnapp.

00:07:32.467 --> 00:07:36.100
-Oh, my God!
-He did it again.

00:07:36.100 --> 00:07:38.033
-My thanks to
Millie Bobby Brown,

00:07:38.033 --> 00:07:41.033
Noah Schnapp.
"Bron-Bron," give me a call.

00:07:41.033 --> 00:07:42.501
We're talking to Millie
after the break.

00:07:42.501 --> 00:07:43.968
Stick around, everybody.
Thank you, Noah!

